Title: Matcher: strip missing Vietnamese facility prefixes and unify mở rộng↔extension
Created: 2026-06-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-03T00:00Z claude created — from the Exp2 FP audit (docs/fp-audit-exp2.md): name-normalization gap is 57 distinct / 152 FP occurrences, all recover to a real reference row once normalized

--- body ---
## Context

The Exp2 false-positive audit (`docs/fp-audit-exp2.md`,
`experiments/derived/exp2_fp_classified.csv`) found that **152 of 640 FP
occurrences (24%)** are pure name-normalization failures: the model name
carries a Vietnamese facility-type prefix the cleaner does not strip, or uses
`mở rộng` where the reference uses `extension`/`MR`. Every one recovers to a real
reference plant once normalized (`new_score ≥ 88`).

`src/aedist/cleaner/config.json:name_drops` currently strips (post diacritic
fold, lower-cased): `^tbkhh`, `^lng`, `^nd`, `power plant`, `thermal`, and
parentheticals. It does **not** strip the single most common prefix
`nhiệt điện` (→ `nhiet dien`), nor `nhà máy` (`nha may`), `đồng phát`
(`dong phat`), or bare `tbk`. And `mở rộng`/`MR` is never unified with the
reference's English `extension`.

Worst offenders (count → reference target, cur_score → new_score):
- Nhiệt điện Bà Rịa (18×) → Bà Rịa GT — 85.7 → 100
- Nhiệt điện Cẩm Phả (11×) → Cam Pha 3 — 87.5 → 100
- NĐ đồng phát Hải Hà 1 (10×) → Hai Ha CHP Phase 1 — 77.8 → 93.3
- Nhiệt điện Na Dương (9×) → Na Dương 1 — 88.9 → 100
- NĐ đồng phát Đức Giang (5×) → Duc Giang – Lao Cai Chemical — 85.7 → 100

The reference change is **zero**: this only edits the cleaner, so existing Exp2
runs can be re-scored in place (no model re-runs).

## Approach

1. Add to `name_drops` (anchored / word-boundary forms, post-fold): `nhiet dien`,
   `nha may`, `dong phat`, `\btbk\b`, `nmnd?`. Keep them order-safe with the
   existing roman-numeral substitution.
2. Add a `name_substitutions` rule unifying the extension marker:
   `mo rong` / `\bmr\b` / `extension` → one canonical token. It must run so the
   downstream unit-number veto in `matching/lp.py` sees identical names.
3. Guard against over-stripping a name to empty (e.g. a row literally named
   "Nhà máy nhiệt điện"): if drops would empty the name, keep the pre-drop form.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `name_drops` strips `nhiet dien`, `nha may`, `dong phat`, bare `tbk`
- [ ] `mở rộng` / `MR` / `extension` collapse to one token before veto
- [ ] No name is reduced to the empty string by the new drops (unit-tested)
- [ ] Re-run `uv run python experiments/scripts/fp_audit_exp2.py`:
      `matcher_fail_normalization` occurrences drop from 152 to ≤ 20
- [ ] No regression in matched plants on any existing run (TP count never drops)
- [ ] `make check` passes

## First failing test
`tests/test_cleaner.py` (red→green): assert
`clean_name("Nhiệt điện Bà Rịa") == clean_name("Bà Rịa")` and
`clean_name("Vĩnh Tân 4 mở rộng") == clean_name("Vinh Tan 4 extension")`.

## Out of scope
- The LP-veto / combined `X & Y` failures (→ 0393).
- Any edit to `data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1.csv` (→ 0394 / 0395).
- Re-running the models — re-scoring existing outputs is enough.

